==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|-}} and {{inh|en|ang|mund}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*mundō||hand, protection, security}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/mʊnd/|/mʌnd/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mund.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mund2.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʊnd|ʌnd|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[hand]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[security|Security]], granted by a king or earl, the violation of which was punished by a [[fine]] (a [[mundbyrd]]).
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[protection|Protection]]; [[guardianship]].

