==Albanian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sq|/ˈmund/}}

===Etymology 1===
{{unc|sq}}: Possibly:
* From {{der|sq|ine-pro|*megʰ-|t=to be able}},<ref>{{R:sq:Çabej St.|vol=1|pages=357–358}}</ref><ref>{{R:sq:Demiraj|mund|281}}</ref> though there's no evidence supporting the fall of the velar.
* A nasal-infixed formation from the root {{m|ine-pro|*mewd-}}, whence also {{m|lt|mudà|t=possibility}}, {{m|lt|mudúoti|t=to try, attempt}} and {{cog|sa|मुद्|t=to be happy, rejoice}}.<ref>{{R:sq:Orel|mund|pages=277–278}}</ref>
* From {{der|sq|ine-pro|*meHndʰ-||to pay attention, wisdom}}.<ref>{{R:sq:Meyer|page=291}}</ref><ref>{{R:sq:SAEW|page=58}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:IEW|head=3. men|page=727}}</ref>
* Akin to {{cog|lt|išmintìs|t=to be able}}, {{m|lt|išmėginti|t=try}}, {{m|lt|išmintìs|t=wisdom}}.<ref>{{cite-book|title=Evidence for Laryngeals|author=Werner Winter|year=1965|oclc=603158404|publisher=The Hague, Mouton|page=138}}</ref>

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|sq|mundënj||Arvanitic|Arbëresh}}
* {{alt|sq|mûj|muj||Gheg}}

====Verb====
{{sq-verb|munda|mundur}}

# {{lb|sq|intransitive}} [[can]], to [[be able to]]; to [[have]] the [[opportunity]], [[power]] or [[ability]]
# {{ng|followed by {{m|sq|të}}}}
## {{ng|grammatical [[particle]] used for [[conjunctive]] forms}}
##: {{ux|sq|A '''mund të''' më tregoni shtëpinë?|'''Could''' you show me the house?}}
## {{lb|sq|third person}} [[could]] be [[possible]]; [[possibly]], [[maybe]], [[perhaps]] {{q|used as a semi-[[auxiliary]] verb}}
# to [[beat]], [[win over]], [[conquer]]
# {{lb|sq|transitive}} to [[defeat]], [[beat]]; to [[emerge]] [[victorious]] {{q|in a match, battle}}
# to [[survive]], [[get]] [[over]], [[beat]] {{q|a fear, illness, disease}}
# {{lb|sq|figurative|third person}} [[take over]] {{q|with short pronoun forms}}
#: {{ux|sq|'''Më mundi''' gjumi.|The sleep '''took over me'''}}
# {{lb|sq|mediopassive|nocat=1}} {{def-see|sq|mundem}}

